window.docContents[141].resolve({"/Storage-and-commands/Local-reference/#Core-C______--Storage-and-commands--Local-reference":{"contents":"The local reference τ& y = e binds a second name to the location e denotes, without allocating. The initialiser must denote a location and have the declared type, and the reference has in  the type of its referent, because every read and write through it is a read or write at the referent. The binding is an alias, not owned, so the exit of the block that declared the reference leaves the location in . A reference to a temporary, to nullptr or to an expression without a location does not exist, and a dangling reference is impossible by construction, because a reference names only locations of enclosing blocks or of objects in the store.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Storage and commands","header":"4.2. Local reference","id":"/Storage-and-commands/Local-reference/#Core-C______--Storage-and-commands--Local-reference"}});